  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Port Management Program - Energy Transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity strengthened cooperation between the Netherlands and India on sustainable port development and the energy transition. A five-day training programme in Rotterdam, organised by the Port of Rotterdam, brought together 15 to 20 senior officials from the Indian maritime sector to exchange knowledge on sustainable port management and the green hydrogen economy.The programme strengthened institutional ties and increased the visibility of the Dutch maritime ecosystem in India, while supporting follow up initiatives on smart and sustainable port development. It also contributed to broader bilateral cooperation, including a Letter of Intent on a Green and Digital Sea Corridor and collaboration on hydrogen storage, transport and bunkering.</narrative>
  </description>
